WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.317
A shopper picks up a box of garbanzo
beans.

00:00:03.317 --> 00:00:07.503
The checkout camera sees the box, a hand,
and the shelf behind them.

00:00:07.823 --> 00:00:13.652
The frozen retriever compares this whole
image with every catalog description.

00:00:13.652 --> 00:00:17.892
The can scores 0.220. The box scores
0.218.

00:00:18.212 --> 00:00:21.353
A difference of two thousandths puts the
wrong package first.

00:00:21.353 --> 00:00:23.865
Where can a reranker learn to distinguish
them?

00:00:24.955 --> 00:00:29.019
As shoppers handle new products, the
store collects more views.

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:31.051
Their product identities are unknown.

00:00:31.051 --> 00:00:33.489
Consider this training photograph of
apples.

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:39.218
Given ten candidate names, the teacher
assigns 86.5% to Royal Gala.

00:00:39.218 --> 00:00:43.153
Adding catalog pictures still leaves
Royal Gala first.

00:00:43.473 --> 00:00:47.660
Both answers are wrong. Should this frame
teach the reranker to recognize

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:48.358
Royal Gala?

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:52.372
A label model treats the product as
unknown.

00:00:52.372 --> 00:00:56.757
It combines the retrieval scores and both
teacher answers with evidence from

00:00:56.757 --> 00:00:57.853
other store frames.

00:00:58.173 --> 00:01:03.027
Each dot is a frame. Its position shows
similarity to two fitted product

00:01:03.027 --> 00:01:05.640
clusters. Follow the ring around our
photograph.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.896
At initialization, Pink Lady has less
than one percent probability.

00:01:10.896 --> 00:01:14.351
After one update it passes ninety
percent.

00:01:14.351 --> 00:01:16.819
After fifteen, it reaches 99.5%.

00:01:17.139 --> 00:01:19.783
The retriever also voted for Pink Lady.

00:01:19.783 --> 00:01:23.560
The frame meets both conditions and
becomes a training example.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.743
The slow thinker learns two projections.

00:01:26.743 --> 00:01:31.626
One maps image patches and the other maps
catalog tokens into the same space.

00:01:31.946 --> 00:01:34.645
For each patch, take its best token
match.

00:01:34.645 --> 00:01:37.343
Moving to a different patch changes the
similarities.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:41.310
Average the best matches across all 576
patches.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:46.325
During training, the inferred target
competes with the other nine entries.

00:01:47.415 --> 00:01:51.852
Return to the box of beans. At checkout
the teacher stays offline.

00:01:51.852 --> 00:01:54.071
The frozen retriever builds a shortlist.

00:01:54.391 --> 00:01:56.676
A single candidate is returned directly.

00:01:56.676 --> 00:02:01.629
An ambiguous frame is reranked only when
the first choice has enough retained

00:02:01.629 --> 00:02:02.391
training targets.

00:02:02.711 --> 00:02:08.087
Here three entries remain. The patch
comparisons put the box first with

00:02:08.087 --> 00:02:08.983
probability 0.92.

00:02:10.073 --> 00:02:16.553
On GroceryVision and Klasson, reranking
raises recall by 12.5 and 17.3

00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:17.731
percentage points.

00:02:18.051 --> 00:02:22.115
On Retail-786k, the gain is 1.1 points.

00:02:22.115 --> 00:02:26.179
TransCLIP with teacher answers reaches
97.0% there.
